lesson: 258
title: Seating and serving the guests
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: At a party every person at the table gets one cup and one plate: that is 2 things for each person.
explain: Do not forget the birthday child: the guests come to the party, and the child having the birthday sits at the table too.
explain: 8 guests and the birthday child are 9 people, and 9 × 2 = 18 cups and plates.
vars: a=name b=name g=4..15
answer: (g + 1) * 2
exercise: {g} guests come to {a}'s birthday party. How many cups and plates must be put out for the guests and {a}?
exercise: It is {a}'s birthday, and {a.he} has invited {g} friends. Everyone at the table gets a cup and a plate. How many cups and plates is that?
exercise: {a}'s mum lays out cups and plates for {g} guests and for the birthday child. How many does she lay out in all?
exercise: {g} children come to {b}'s party. How many paper cups and paper plates are needed for all the children at the table, {b} too?
exercise: The birthday child and {g} guests sit down to eat. How many cups and plates are on the table?
exercise: {g} kids coming to {a}'s party + {a} of course. cups and plates how many
exercise: birthday party for {a}, {g+1}, no wait {g} mates invited. how many cups n plates altogether
exercise: {g} guests at the party, the clown costs heaps btw, and the birthday kid too. cups and plates?
exercise: {a}'s having {g} friends round for {a.his} bday. how many plates and cups do we need
exercise: set out cups n plates for {g} guests and the birthday girl pls. how many is that
test: How many cups and plates are needed in total for a birthday child and {g} guests?
test: {b} counts the plates and cups for {a}'s party, where {g} invited children join {a} at the table. What number does {b} get?
test: For the birthday tea, cups and plates are set for all {g} visitors and for the child whose birthday it is. How many items is that?
test: {g} guests + bday kid. cups and plates?
test: {a} says {g*2} cups n plates is enough for {g} guests. forgot someone. how many really
test: party for {a}, {g} friends coming, {b} brings {g} balloons. how many cups and plates for everyone eating
exam: It is given that {g.words} guests attend a birthday celebration in addition to the person whose birthday is being celebrated. Determine the aggregate number of cups and plates to be provided.
exam: A birthday luncheon is attended by {g} invitees and the celebrant. Ascertain the total quantity of cups and plates requisite for all those seated.
exam: Compute the number of cups and plates necessitated by a party at which {g} guests are seated together with the child whose birthday it is.
exam: Whereas {g} children have accepted an invitation to the birthday of {a}, state the total number of cups and plates to be laid for all persons present at table.
exercise: {a} invited {g+1} friends, but one of them was unwell, so {g} came. Everyone at the table, {a} too, gets a cup and a plate. How many cups and plates are put out?
exercise: {g} mates turning up to {a}'s birthday, not {b} though, {b.his} mum says {b.he}'s grounded, tough luck. cup and plate for each guest and {a}, how many's that?
test: {a}'s goldfish went to the great pond in the sky last week, but {g} guests still come to {a.his} party. Each guest and {a} get a cup and a plate. How many items is that?
